    const Section(
      title: 'Physical Examination Findings:',
      content: '**Vitals**: BP 134/84 mmHg, HR 74 bpm, Temp 36.8C, BMI 30.\n\n**Cervical Spine and Upper Extremity Examination**:\n- **Inspection**: Mild loss of cervical lordosis. Forward head posture. Rounded shoulders. No visible atrophy.\n- **Cervical ROM**: Flexion 40 degrees (mildly limited), extension 30 degrees (moderately limited, reproduces arm pain), right lateral flexion 25 degrees (limited, painful), right rotation 45 degrees (limited, reproduces radiating arm pain). Left ROM relatively preserved.\n- **Palpation**: Paravertebral muscle spasm right > left at C5-C6 level. Tenderness over right C6 facet joint.\n\n**Provocative Tests**:\n- **Spurling test**: Positive on the right — axial compression with extension and right lateral flexion reproduces shooting pain into the right thumb. This is the hallmark exam finding for cervical radiculopathy (specificity 93%, sensitivity 30-50%).\n- **Shoulder abduction relief sign**: Positive — placing the right hand on top of the head reduces the radiating arm pain by relieving traction on the C6 nerve root.\n- **Neck distraction test**: Positive — manual axial distraction reduces arm pain.\n- **Lhermitte sign**: Negative (important — argues against myelopathy).\n\n**Neurologic Exam**:\n- **Motor**: Right biceps 4/5 (C5-C6), right wrist extensors (extensor carpi radialis) 4/5 (C6), right triceps 5/5 (C7), right grip 5/5. Left upper extremity 5/5 throughout. Lower extremities 5/5 bilaterally.\n- **Reflexes**: Right biceps (C5-C6) 1+ (diminished compared to left 2+). Right brachioradialis 1+. Triceps 2+ bilaterally. Patellar and Achilles reflexes 2+ bilaterally. No pathologic reflexes (Hoffman negative bilaterally, Babinski negative bilaterally).\n- **Sensation**: Decreased light touch and pinprick over the right lateral forearm and thumb (C6 dermatome). Intact in all other distributions.\n- **Coordination**: Intact finger-to-nose bilaterally. No upper extremity drift. Rapid alternating movements normal.\n- **Gait**: Normal. Tandem gait normal. No spasticity. (Myelopathy screening negative.)\n\n**Shoulder examination**: Full ROM bilaterally, negative impingement signs, negative rotator cuff weakness — important to rule out shoulder pathology masquerading as cervical radiculopathy.',
